# End-to-end testing

- Use Playwright in `portfolio-website/e2e`. Spec files end with `.spec.ts`.
- Chromium only. Do not add Firefox or WebKit projects unless asked.
- Three projects, all Chromium: `chromium` (Desktop Chrome), `mobile-chromium` (Pixel 7), and `small-mobile-chromium` (Galaxy S8). Specs must pass on all three.
- `npm test` runs every project. Use `test:chrome` or `test:mobile` to narrow while debugging.
- Prefer role, label, and accessible name locators over CSS or test ids. Layout assertions may use class selectors when geometry is the thing under test.
- Put a positive assertion (element is visible) before a negative one.
- Reuse helpers in `e2e/helpers/` (for example `goToHome`, and `boxOf` / `lastLineOf` / `overlaps` / `horizontalOverflow` for layout) instead of duplicating navigation or geometry maths.
- Never assert an inline element's `boundingBox` against a single line. Font metrics differ between Windows and the Ubuntu CI runner, so text wraps at different widths and `boundingBox` returns the union of every line. Use `lastLineOf` for the line under test.
- Keep responsive regressions covered in `layout.spec.ts`: no horizontal overflow, the sidebar must never overlap `<main>`, and on desktop the 42rem reading column is centred in the viewport.
- Accessibility: `a11y.spec.ts` runs `@axe-core/playwright` with tags `wcag2a`, `wcag2aa`, and `wcag22aa` on home, each collection route, a blog post, and the heatmap. Exclude only third-party chrome (Leaflet). Axe is not full WCAG compliance.
- If a test fails, fix the test first. Do not change product behaviour to make a test pass unless the owner agrees there is a product bug.
- `npm test` in `portfolio-website` is the command for local and CI. Playwright builds and previews the site via `webServer`.
- `webServer` reuses an existing server locally. Kill a stale `vite preview` on port 4173 before trusting a run, or it will test an old build.
- Mixed-case routes such as `/Portfolio/Blogs` are covered in `e2e/canonical-url.spec.ts`. Vite preview rewrites those to the SPA entry so the run matches GitHub Pages serving `404.html`.
